<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_PA-192.2-ev-alt-fuel-fleet-operations-charging-and-energy-management" targetNamespace="https://erpplans.local/bpmn" exporter="erpplans generate-bpmn.py" exporterVersion="1.0">
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5473" name="W5473. EV Fleet Daily Charging Operations, Load Scheduling &amp; Smart-Charge Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vehicles in service; nightly/peak charging cycles
Frequency: Daily, per vehicle and per depot
Volume: Per EV in the owned fleet, daily; scales with conversion (~early tens → larger)
Owner: Fleet Charging Operations Supervisor (VS-06)
Participants: Drivers, Facilities/Energy (VS-138/VS-120), Depot/DC Ops (VS-04), EV-host ops (VS-163)
Source: workflow W5473 — EV Fleet Daily Charging Operations, Load Scheduling &amp; Smart-Charge Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5473_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5473_Lane1" name="Charge Ops Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5473_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5473_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5473_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5473_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5473_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5473_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5473_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5473_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5473_Start4" name="Vehicles in service; nightly/peak charging cycles">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5473_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5473_Task5" name="Each evening, the charge-management system schedules each returning EV against…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Each evening, the charge-management system schedules each returning EV against its next-day dispatch (W5477), state-of-charge, time-of-departure, and the site&#x27;s transformer/charger capacity (W5468).
Responsible (R): Charge Ops Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): Fleet Charging Operations Supervisor
Duration: nightly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5473_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5473_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5473_Task6" name="Apply smart-charging rules: prioritize low-tariff / high-renewable hours…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Apply smart-charging rules: prioritize low-tariff / high-renewable hours (W5479), cap simultaneous draw to the site limit, defer non-urgent charging, and sequence to avoid peak-demand charges.
Responsible (R): Charge Ops Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): Fleet Charging Operations Supervisor
Duration: nightly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5473_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5473_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5473_Task7" name="Reconcile fleet-charging priority vs the shared customer-host network (VS-163)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Reconcile fleet-charging priority vs the shared customer-host network (VS-163) under a documented priority policy (fleet-priority off-hours, customer-priority during trading).
Responsible (R): Charge Ops Supervisor
Accountable (A): Fleet Charging Operations Supervisor
Duration: ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5473_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5473_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5473_Task8" name="Log every charging session (vehicle, charger, kWh, start/stop, tariff…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Log every charging session (vehicle, charger, kWh, start/stop, tariff, renewable-share) for billing (W5486), MRV (W5481), and analytics (W5488).
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Fleet Charging Operations Supervisor
Duration: per session</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5473_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5473_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5473_Task9" name="Exception-handle charging failures (faulty charger, vehicle not accepting…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Exception-handle charging failures (faulty charger, vehicle not accepting charge, interrupted session) and trigger maintenance (W5474) or diesel/hybrid fallback (W5477).
Responsible (R): Charge Ops Supervisor
Accountable (A): Fleet Charging Operations Supervisor
Duration: per exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5473_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5473_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5473_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5473_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5473_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-807 (ensure controlled execution — EV / Alt-Fuel Fleet Operations, Charging &amp; Energy Management (PA-192.2).) | - operational: documented fleet-vs-customer priority policy; SoC-at-departure minimum enforced.
Owner: Fleet Charging Operations Supervisor (VS-06)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5473_Assoc12" sourceRef="W5473_Annotation11" targetRef="W5473_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5473_Flow13" sourceRef="W5473_Start4" targetRef="W5473_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5473_Flow14" sourceRef="W5473_Task5" targetRef="W5473_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5473_Flow15" sourceRef="W5473_Task6" targetRef="W5473_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5473_Flow16" sourceRef="W5473_Task7" targetRef="W5473_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5473_Flow17" sourceRef="W5473_Task8" targetRef="W5473_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5473_Flow18" sourceRef="W5473_Task9" targetRef="W5473_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
