    <bpmn:process id="W_W5475" name="W5475. EV Battery State-of-Health, Range Assurance &amp; Battery Lifecycle Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vehicles in service; periodic SoH review; warranty/degradation thresholds
Frequency: Continuous SoH telemetry; quarterly SoH review per vehicle
Volume: Per EV in the fleet
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Manager (VS-06.2)
Participants: OEM/battery vendor, Telematics (VS-06), Maintenance (VS-06.2), Treasury/warranty (W5467)
Source: workflow W5475 — EV Battery State-of-Health, Range Assurance &amp; Battery Lifecycle Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5475_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5475_Lane1" name="Telematics">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5475_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5475_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5475_Lane2" name="Maintenance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5475_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5475_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5475_Lane3" name="Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5475_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5475_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5475_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5475_Start5" name="Vehicles in service; periodic SoH review; warranty/degradation thresholds">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5475_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5475_Task6" name="Capture battery SoH telemetry (capacity fade, internal resistance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Capture battery SoH telemetry (capacity fade, internal resistance, cell-balance, temperature excursions, charge-cycle count) from the vehicle BMS via telematics (VS-06).
Responsible (R): Telematics / Maintenance Analyst
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5475_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5475_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5475_Task7" name="Track each vehicle&#x27;s usable range vs its dispatch requirement (W5477); flag…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Track each vehicle&#x27;s usable range vs its dispatch requirement (W5477); flag vehicles approaching range-insufficiency for route reassignment or remediation.
Responsible (R): Maintenance Analyst
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5475_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5475_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5475_Task8" name="Detect degradation against the OEM warranty threshold (e.g., &lt;70% at…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Detect degradation against the OEM warranty threshold (e.g., &lt;70% at 5-yr/300k-km per W5467) and prepare warranty claims / battery-module replacement cases.
Responsible (R): Maintenance / Warranty Admin
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: per threshold</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5475_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5475_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5475_Task9" name="Manage the battery lifecycle plan: in-service → degradation monitoring →…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Manage the battery lifecycle plan: in-service → degradation monitoring → warranty/replacement → second-life (W5487) → recycling (W5487), maintaining a battery passport/traceability record.
Responsible (R): Maintenance Analyst
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5475_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5475_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5475_Task10" name="Maintain battery thermal-management discipline (avoid chronic high-temp…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Maintain battery thermal-management discipline (avoid chronic high-temp operation that accelerates degradation in the PH tropical climate) and feed any thermal event into the safety program (W5483).
Responsible (R): Maintenance / Driver
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
