    <bpmn:process id="W_W5480" name="W5480. EV-Specific Preventive Maintenance, Diagnostics, Roadside &amp; Towing Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vehicle in service; PM schedule; fault/roadside event
Frequency: Per OEM PM schedule; per fault/event
Volume: Per EV/alt-fuel vehicle in the fleet
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Manager (VS-06.2)
Participants: Maintenance technicians, OEM authorized service, Towing/roadside vendor, HSE (VS-24)
Source: workflow W5480 — EV-Specific Preventive Maintenance, Diagnostics, Roadside &amp; Towing Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5480_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5480_Lane1" name="Maintenance Technician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5480_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5480_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5480_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5480_Lane2" name="Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5480_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5480_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5480_Lane3" name="Towing Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5480_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5480_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5480_Start5" name="Vehicle in service; PM schedule; fault/roadside event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5480_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5480_Task6" name="Execute EV-specific preventive maintenance per OEM schedule…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Execute EV-specific preventive maintenance per OEM schedule (battery/thermal-system inspection, high-voltage isolation test, inverter/motor, regenerative-brake system, cooling-fluid, 12V aux) distinct from diesel PM.
Responsible (R): Maintenance Technician
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: per schedule</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5480_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5480_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5480_Task7" name="Diagnose faults via OBD/EV telematics (fault codes, HV-system warnings, thermal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Diagnose faults via OBD/EV telematics (fault codes, HV-system warnings, thermal events) and triage to in-house (light), OEM authorized (HV/battery), or roadside/tow.
Responsible (R): Maintenance Technician / OEM
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: per fault</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5480_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5480_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5480_Task8" name="Maintain a trained/authorized technician pool (HV-qualified per OEM + DOLE-OSH)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Maintain a trained/authorized technician pool (HV-qualified per OEM + DOLE-OSH) and OEM tooling; outsource HV/battery work to authorized service where in-house qualification is absent.
Responsible (R): Maintenance / HR (VS-19.4)
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5480_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5480_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5480_Task9" name="Operate roadside assistance and towing for EVs: HV-safe towing (no flat-tow of…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Operate roadside assistance and towing for EVs: HV-safe towing (no flat-tow of driven axle), recovery of a stranded/thermal-event vehicle, and coordination with the towing vendor (links VS-56/VS-74).
Responsible (R): Towing Vendor / Fleet
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5480_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5480_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5480_Task10" name="Feed all safety-relevant faults (thermal runaway signs, isolation loss, fire)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Feed all safety-relevant faults (thermal runaway signs, isolation loss, fire) into the battery-fire/HV safety program (W5483) and the recall path if systemic.
Responsible (R): Maintenance / HSE
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5480_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5480_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5480_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5480_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5480_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-807 (ensure controlled execution — EV / Alt-Fuel Fleet Operations, Charging &amp; Energy Management (PA-192.2).) | - operational: HV-qualification gating before HV work; HV-safe towing protocol mandatory; thermal-event response per W5483.
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Manager (VS-06.2)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
